# Sidequest: Catch a Fish: at Bot1's turn 3 upkeep the top card is a Plains, so nothing is asked and it is drawn. At turn 5
# Bot1 is asked of an Ornithopter (an artifact creature) and declines: it stays on top, is drawn, and the enchantment does
# not transform (the 2025-06-06 ruling). At turn 7 Bot1 reveals Grizzly Bears (a creature that is no
# artifact) and puts it into its hand: a Food token, and the
# enchantment transforms (CR 701.27a) into Cooking Campsite. Its "{3}, {T}, Sacrifice an artifact" is refused in the
# beginning of combat step (sorcery speed, CR 602.5d) and in the second main phase taken off three Moxen, the pool empty
# after, sacrificing the Food: a +1/+1 counter on each creature Bot1 controls, Savannah Lions and Ornithopter, and none on
# Bot2's Ornithopter (CR 122.6). On turn 9 the Campsite taps for {W}.

